  "close_rendering": "You shall not take vengeance and you shall not bear a grudge against the sons of your people, and you shall love your neighbour as yourself. I am the LORD.",
  "whats_happening": "This is the last of a run of short commands about how Israelites should treat one another. It moves from two things not to do to one thing to do. In the Hebrew, the famous second half is joined to the first. So the love commanded here is set against revenge and grudges, not described as a feeling. The verse ends by naming the speaker rather than giving a reason.",
  "key_words": [
    {
      "surface": "וְאָֽהַבְתָּ֥",
      "lemma": "אָהַב",
      "gloss": "and you shall love",
      "note": "This verb form carries on the two 'you shall not' commands before it, rather than starting something new.",
      "strongs": "H0157"
    },
    {
      "surface": "לְרֵעֲךָ֖",
      "lemma": "רֵעַ",
      "gloss": "to your neighbour",
      "note": "One written word carrying three morphemes: preposition, noun in construct, and a second person suffix.",
